# Law Pipeline — Source URLs
# ============================
# Add one URL per line. Empty lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# The fetcher auto-detects the source type from the URL:
#
#   1. gesetze-im-internet.de (GII XML)
#      URL format: https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/<slug>/xml.zip
#      Example:     https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/vgv_2017/xml.zip
#      Returns: ZIP with one XML file using the GII norm DTD.
#
#   2. verwaltungsvorschriften-im-internet.de (VV HTML)
#      URL format: https://www.verwaltungsvorschriften-im-internet.de/<doc>.htm
#      Returns: Semi-structured HTML with paragraph markers.
#
#   3. eur-lex.europa.eu (EUR-Lex CELLAR)
#      URL format: https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/DE/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:<CELEX_NUMBER>
#      Example:     https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/DE/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:02014L0024-20260101
#      The fetcher auto-rewrites this to the CELLAR API at publications.europa.eu
#      to bypass the EUR-Lex WAF block.
#
#   4. gesetze.berlin.de (BSBE XML)
#      URL format: https://gesetze.berlin.de/perma?j=<LAW_ABBREVIATION>
#      Example:     https://gesetze.berlin.de/perma?j=VergabeG_BE
#      Returns: GII norm DTD XML (uses perma redirect + AIZ ZIP download).
#      Requires HTTP/2. The law abbreviation (j=) maps to the law's jurisdiction ID.
#
# Add your URLs below this line:

# --- Examples (one per supported source type) ---

# GII XML
# https://www.gesetze-im-internet.de/vgv_2017/xml.zip

# VV HTML
# https://www.verwaltungsvorschriften-im-internet.de/example_doc.htm

# EUR-Lex (CELLAR)
# https://eur-lex.europa.eu/legal-content/DE/TXT/HTML/?uri=CELEX:02016R0679-20160504

# BSBE (gesetze.berlin.de, requires HTTP/2)
# https://gesetze.berlin.de/perma?j=VergabeG_BE
